|~ `::link`, the kind of a link, and what is declared under it: the verb
   that opens the page a link names.
   The rules it holds: [QSDSP#residence], [QSSLF#doc]. ~|

:link
  |~~ A link names a page for its reader to follow: written in the prose
      of a doc as a quote under this tag whose code answers the name the
      page is under, `::link~(::vec/sort)`, which `open` opens, so
      `::vec | doc | links | map open` answers the pages the page of
      vectors names. Links make the pages a hypertext: a page names the
      pages that go deeper.

      A link opens a page, every link of the catalog among them; a query
      that lists or shows something is a snippet, and one that answers
      true a law. A link is a quote under a stack of tags that holds
      `::link`, the stack read from the outside in, so a tag a host or a
      reader lays over a link keeps it a link, and its code runs by
      `answer` as the code of any quote does.
      ::snippet~(::qlang | doc | links) lists the links of the first page.
      ::link~(::link/open) ::link~(::snippet) ::link~(::qlang/hypertext)
  ~~|
  ::kind
    | accepts
        |~~ The code that names the page, a quote, or a snippet, which the
            link makes a link as well.
        ~~|
        #[::quote ::snippet]
    | throws :PayloadKindNotTakenError
        |~~ A link holds the code that names its page, a quote, or a
            snippet, `::link~(::qlang)`; a quote under another tag gives the
            quote beneath by `payload`.
        ~~|
    | proves :isALink
        |~~ A link a doc holds is a `::link`. ~~|
        ~(|~~ ::link~(::qlang/values) ~~| | links | first | tag | eq ::link)
    | proves :opensToPages
        |~~ The links of the first page open to pages. ~~|
        ~(::qlang | doc | links | map open | every (tag | eq ::doc))
    | proves :holdsUnderAStackOfTags
        |~~ A quote under a stack of tags holding `::link` is a link. ~~|
        ~(|~~ ::Host::link~(::vec) ~~| | links | count | eq 1)
    | proves :PayloadKindNotTakenError/refusesANumber
        |~~ A link is a quote. ~~|
        ~(::link#5 !| tag | eq ::link/PayloadKindNotTakenError)
    | proves :staysASnippetUnderIt
        |~~ A quote under a link and a snippet is both. ~~|
        ~(|~~ a ::link::snippet~(::vec) b ~~| | get [(links | count) (snippets | count)] | eq [1 1]);

:link/open
  |~~ Answers the page the link names, the doc of the name its code
      answers: `|~~ See ::link~(::vec/sort). ~~| | links | first | open`
      answers the page of `::vec/sort`, and `links | map open` reads every
      page a page names in one query. The code runs as `answer` runs it,
      and a link whose code answers a value that names no page opens the
      page of its kind, as `doc` reads one.
      ::link~(::quote/answer) ::link~(::any/doc) ::link~(::doc/links)
  ~~|
  ::fn
    | returns |~~ The page the link names. ~~| ::doc
    | throws :SubjectNotLinkError
        |~~ `open` opens the page a link names; the code of a quote that is
            no link answers by `answer`, `~(1 | add 1) | answer`.
        ~~|
    | proves :opensThePageItNames
        |~~ A link opens the page of the name its code answers. ~~|
        ~(|~~ See ::link~(::vec/sort). ~~| | links | first | open | eq (::vec/sort | doc))
    | proves :answersTheNameItHolds
        |~~ The code of a link answers the name it holds, beneath the page
            `open` reads there.
        ~~|
        ~(|~~ See ::link~(::vec/sort). ~~| | links | first | get [answer (open | tag)] | eq [::vec/sort ::doc])
    | proves :SubjectNotLinkError/refusesAQuote
        |~~ A quote that is no link names no page to open. ~~|
        ~(~(1 | add 1) | open !| tag | eq ::link/open/SubjectNotLinkError)
    | impl ~(answer | doc);
